rth is over two  billion dollars and he currently  dedicates his time and resources to  making the world a better safer place  for future generations  by committing himself to becoming a  success and by working hard Ted Turner  was able to turn his father's bankrupt  company around and become one of the  wealthiest entrepreneurs in the world to  help you turn your company around here  are three action items you can learn  from Ted Turner action item number one  decide you'll be a success a turning  point for many entrepreneurs comes when  they commit to their business and decide  that they are going to see things  through until they become a success it  doesn't mean that it's going to happen  overnight but it's a commitment to  reaching success I'm putting the daily  effort into making that goal become a  reality stunned by his father's suicide  turn and realize that he had to set  ambitious goals for himself so he always  had something to live for he committed  to changing his path and getting serious  about his life despite advice a sell-off  Turner advertising after his father's  death turn her fought to keep the  company and work to bringing enough  business to pay off its debts as he grew  his business he kept driving for higher  goals to keep himself challenged and  gave his best effort every day according  to Turner if you've got an innovative  idea and the majority doesn't poopoo it  then odds are you must not have a very  good idea when people thought I was  loony it didn't bother me at all in fact  I considered that I must be really onto  something you should set goals beyond  your reach so you always have something  to live for I decided I wanted to be a  success  oxana number two never quit when you're  an entrepreneur there's always a  temptation to quit when the excitement  of starting up wears off and near the  daily grind in front in your business  don't quit remember you decided that  you're going to be successful and that  comes from doing something every day  that will move your business forward  remember why you started your business  and think about all the people you're  going to be able to help find that  motivation to keep going even when  people around you think you're nuts  almost every venture that Turner started  up for every business that he acquired  critics told him that it would never  work and he was spending his money  foolishly when Turner told people he  wanted to create a 24-hour news only  network they thought he was crazy nobody  would tune in to watch news all day long  it was a suicide mission they said  undeterred Turner fought tooth and nail  until he finally launched CNN which  revolutionized the media industry and  became a rapid success according to  Turner all my life people have said that  I wasn't going to make it they laughed  at me when i started with CBS they  laughed at me when i started CNN they  laughed at me when I bought the Braves  they laughed at me when I bought the  Hawks they laughed at me when I bought  MGM you can never quit winners never  quit and quitters never win action item  number three work hard there are many  paths of success but one common theme  you'll find if you model successful  entrepreneurs is that they worked very  hard to get their businesses going being  an entrepreneur is not a nine-to-five  job you're going to work harder than  you've ever worked before and will  hopefully love almost every minute of it  because you're doing something that  you're extremely passionate about  success does not come without the hard  work behind it when Turner was launching  CNN he frequently worked 18-hour days he  converted his office into an apartment  and slept over most nights at CNN  headquarters CNN staff regularly saw him  leave his office to grab a cup coffee in  his bathrobe Turner felt that the best  way to lead is by example and inspired  his staff to work almost as hard as him  to achieve their common goal  a former employee one set of Turner he  was much more than a cheerleader he was  a kind of guy you'd want to run through  a wall for according to Turner early to  bed early to rise work like hell and  advertise CNN came out of my heart and  soul I see what keeps people young work  so remember decide you're going to be a  success never quit and work hard to  finish up this video I wanted to share  one of my favorite true stories about  Ted Turner and some of his best quotes  Turner has a long-standing bitterness  with News Corporation's Rupert Murdoch  it began in nineteen eighty-three when a  Murdock sponsored yacht crashed in the  Turner's boat during a race causing it  to sink only 10 kilometers from the  finish line Turner was an avid sailor  and won the American Cup sailings most  prestigious award so he took the crash  personally he challenged Murdoch to a  televised fist fight in Las Vegas  Murdock declined  thank you for joining me for another  edition of model in the Masters if you  like the video and want to see more  please leave a thumbs up below I'd also  love to hear feedback if you want to  leave a comment under the video and stay  tuned for the next episode
 

